description:
Captures and analyzes the screen or webcam image. MUST be called when user asks what is on screen, what you see, analyze my screen, look at camera, etc. You have NO visual ability without this tool. LAST RESORT for reading content: files, web pages and system state must be read directly first (file_processor, browser_control get_text, computer_control running_apps/system_snapshot); use this only when that is impossible or the user explicitly asks you to look at the screen/camera. This tool returns screen/camera analysis text as the tool result. Use the returned analysis to answer the user. 

For normal analysis: {"text": "What do you see?", "angle": "screen"}. action="screen" is accepted as an alias for normal analysis.
For async: {"text": "Analyze my screen", "async": true}
For latest result: {"action": "result", "request_id": "latest"}
For list: {"action": "list"}
Other actions: 'list' to see pending requests, 'clear' to clean up.
